                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Shovel Knight is a very well done old-school action platformer with enough balancing and modern mechanisms to remove the tedium of old NES games of the genre.\n\nIt's a recommandation, BUT! 40€ is far too expensive for a game with NES graphics and gameplay. And if you want to get all achievements, you'll have to play five times every game... Erk!\n\nThat said, all four main games are cool.\n\n- Shovel of Hope leans on the easy side, which I don't see as a negative, but the first few levels might appear a bit dull because of it. It really becomes more interesting, so don't give up.\n\n- Plague of Shadows is far more interesting, but maybe a bit too original in its gameplay. I liked it, but I can see how Plague Knight's moveset might deter a casual gamer. This creates a big difficulty spike after Shovel of Hope.\nAlso, you're just playing the same levels as Shovel of Hope. Even if you enjoy the gameplay, this removes all sense of discovery.\n\n- Specter of Torment is my favorite. Shorter, with an intuitive and fast gameplay.\n\n- King of Cards is very cool too. More ambitious, with an original gameplay, lots of optional levels, and a very funny card minigame that is entirely optional if it's not your thing.\n\n- Sadly, sadly! There is a fifth game in the lot...\nShowdown feels like an afterthought. On paper, a multiplayer with 20 different characters looked very cool. \nExcept it's so chaotic it feels completely random. \nThere is no explanation for anything (game modes, map specifities, character movesets, options). \nThe menu is a nightmare to navigate because one of the four default control mappings is selected and the game doesn't tell you which.\nLosing in story mode will ask you if you want to continue or not. Answering either yes or no will send you back to the main menu (some incredibly tight beta-testing there).\n\nTLDR: If you enjoy old-school action platforming, Shovel Knight is a very good choice, but only if you can get it at a (big!) discount.",
